1
00:03:41,538 --> 00:03:47,538
Judgement is coming.

2
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:29,076
Dredd is a action, science fiction film directed by Pete Travis.

3
00:11:04,615 --> 00:11:10,615
In the future, America is a dystopian wasteland.

4
00:14:46,153 --> 00:14:52,153
The latest scourge is Ma-Ma, a prostitute-turned-drug pusher with a
dangerous new drug and aims to take over the city.

5
00:18:27,692 --> 00:18:33,692
The only possibility of stopping her is an elite group of urban police called Judges, who combine
the duties of judge, jury and executioner to deliver a brutal brand of swift justice.

6
00:22:09,230 --> 00:22:15,230
But even the top-ranking Judge, Dredd, discovers that taking down Ma-Ma isn’t as easy as
it seems in this explosive adaptation of the hugely popular comic series.

7
00:25:50,769 --> 00:25:56,769
Judge Dredd, played by Karl Urban.

8
00:29:32,307 --> 00:29:38,307
Cassandra Anderson, played by Olivia Thirlby.

9
00:33:13,846 --> 00:33:19,846
Ma-Ma, played by Lena Headey.

10
00:36:55,384 --> 00:37:01,384
Kay, played by Wood Harris.

11
00:40:36,923 --> 00:40:42,923
Judge Lex, played by Langley Kirkwood.

12
00:44:18,461 --> 00:44:24,461
Ma-Ma Bodyguard, played by Tamer Burjaq.

13
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Dredd is a 2012 science fiction and action film directed by Pete
Travis and written and produced by Alex Garland.

14
00:51:41,538 --> 00:51:47,538
It is based on the 2000 AD comic strip Judge Dredd and its eponymous
character created by John Wagner and Carlos Ezquerra.

15
00:55:23,076 --> 00:55:29,076
Karl Urban stars as Judge Dredd, a law enforcer given the power of judge, jury, and executioner in a
vast, dystopic metropolis called Mega-City One that lies in a post-apocalyptic wasteland.

16
00:59:04,615 --> 00:59:10,615
Dredd and his rookie partner, Judge Anderson (Olivia Thirlby), are forced to bring order to a 200-storey
high-rise block of apartments and deal with its resident drug lord, Ma-Ma (Lena Headey).

17
01:02:46,153 --> 01:02:52,153
Garland began writing the script in 2006, although the development of a new Judge Dredd film
adaptation, unrelated to the 1995 film Judge Dredd, was not announced until December 2008.

18
01:06:27,692 --> 01:06:33,692
Produced by British studio DNA Films, Dredd began principal
photography, using 3D cameras throughout, in November 2010.

19
01:10:09,230 --> 01:10:15,230
Filming took place on practical sets and
locations in Cape Town and Johannesburg.

20
01:13:50,769 --> 01:13:56,769
Dredd was released on 7 September 2012 in the United
Kingdom and on 21 September worldwide.

21
01:17:32,307 --> 01:17:38,307
Critics were generally positive about the film's visual effects, casting and action sequences, while criticism focused on
excessive violence as well as a perceived lack of the satirical elements that are found in the source comic.

22
01:21:13,846 --> 01:21:19,846
Despite the positive critical response, the film earned just over $41 million
at the box office on an estimated budget of $30–45 million.

23
01:24:55,384 --> 01:25:01,384
The theatrical gross made a sequel unlikely, but home media sales and fan efforts endorsed by 2000
AD's publisher Rebellion Developments have maintained the possibility of a second film.

24
01:28:36,923 --> 01:28:42,923
The film explores themes of metropolis, corruption, police, judge, gangster.

25
01:32:18,461 --> 01:32:24,461
The tone is dark and thought_provoking.
